 ],
 "text": "an extract against malaria kept failing. Two yoyo found out why. What was ruining it? It was made with heat. An ancient recipe said, soak the herb, ring out the juice, no biling. Her team extracted it cool in ether. In 1971, it cleared parasites in mice. That led to art amissin' in, and a 2015 Nobel Prize. Lesson, when a good idea fails, test the step you assumed was harmless. Download RM to support livelihood tools."
